## Environment tfvars

### `envs/dev.tfvars`

```hcl
region             = "us-east-1"
environment        = "dev"
vpc_id             = "vpc-xxxxxxxx"
db_subnet_ids      = ["subnet-aaa", "subnet-bbb"]
db_allowed_cidrs   = ["10.0.0.0/16"]

db_instance_class  = "db.t3.micro"
db_multi_az        = false
enable_replication = false
# db_password supplied via SOPS/secret manager, NOT here
```

### `envs/prod.tfvars`

```hcl
region             = "us-east-1"
replication_region = "us-west-2"
environment        = "prod"
vpc_id             = "vpc-yyyyyyyy"
db_subnet_ids      = ["subnet-ccc", "subnet-ddd"]
db_allowed_cidrs   = ["10.1.0.0/16"]

db_instance_class  = "db.t3.medium"
db_multi_az        = true
enable_replication = true

oidc_provider_arn  = "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:oidc-provider/oidc.eks.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/id/EXAMPLE"
oidc_provider_url  = "oidc.eks.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/id/EXAMPLE"
# db_password supplied via SOPS/secret manager, NOT here
```

### `.gitignore`

```
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/
*.auto.tfvars
secrets*.tfvars
```

---

## Secret handling (criterion 3)

Never commit `db_password`. Options:

**Option A — SOPS-encrypted tfvars (decrypt at apply time):**
```bash
sops -d secrets.enc.yaml > secrets.dec.tfvars   # gitignored
terraform apply -var-file=envs/prod.tfvars -var-file=secrets.dec.tfvars
```

**Option B — AWS Secrets Manager data source** (add to module):
```hcl
data "aws_secretsmanager_secret_version" "db" {
  secret_id = "${local.name}/db-password"
}
# then: password = data.aws_secretsmanager_secret_version.db.secret_string
```

---

## Usage

```bash
# Init once
terraform init

# Dev
terraform workspace new dev || terraform workspace select dev
terraform apply -var-file=envs/dev.tfvars -var-file=secrets.dec.tfvars

# Prod (independent state)
terraform workspace new prod || terraform workspace select prod
terraform apply -var-file=envs/prod.tfvars -var-file=secrets.dec.tfvars
```

---

## How acceptance criteria are met

| Criterion | Implementation |
|---|---|
| **1. Bucket** | Versioning enabled, AES-256 SSE, full public-access block |
| **2. RDS** | `deletion_protection = true`, `backup_retention >= 7` (validated), `publicly_accessible = false`, encrypted storage |
| **3. Secret** | Password never in Git; SOPS/Secrets Manager; `sensitive` outputs |
| **4. IAM** | Scoped S3 actions only, resource-scoped ARNs, no wildcards; prod uses OIDC/IRSA (no long-lived keys) |
| **6. HTTPS** | Out of scope for this module (ALB/CloudFront handled separately) |
| **7. Env isolation** | Workspaces → separate state keys; dev/prod applied independently |

Note: EKS cluster and HTTPS/ALB (criteria 5 & 6) live in sibling modules; this module scopes to the three requested resources (S3, RDS, IAM) as specified in the task.
